                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output_collection name="projects" type="list" count="0"/>
            <output_collection name="logs" type="list" count="1">
                <element name="10.5281_zenodo.17533355" ftype="txt">
                    <assert_contents>
                        <has_text text="NOMAD project zip: no (no converted raw file)"/>
                        <has_text text="const_dos_No14_003.sxm: failed (no_result)"/>
                    </assert_contents>
                </element>
            </output_collection>
        </test>
        <!-- Test 03: an empty run gives empty results and no zips or logs. -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="4">
            <param name="manifest" value="manifest_empty.json" ftype="json"/>
            <param name="statuses">
                <collection type="list"/>
            </param>
            <param name="nexus_files">
                <collection type="list"/>
            </param>
            <param name="elns">
                <collection type="list"/>
            </param>
            <param name="raw_files">
                <collection type="list"/>
            </param>
            <param name="context_files">
                <collection type="list"/>
            </param>
            <output name="results" ftype="json">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="&quot;files&quot;: []"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
            <output_collection name="projects" type="list" count="0"/>
            <output_collection name="logs" type="list" count="0"/>
            <output name="summary" ftype="html">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_text text="No records in this run."/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
**What it does**

The last step of the Zenodo → Galaxy → NOMAD harvest. It collects the results of the NeXus
converter for all raw files of a run and builds what the NOMAD side
([nomad-eosc-galaxy-actions](https://github.com/FAIRmat-NFDI/nomad-eosc-galaxy-actions)) reads.
All collections are joined by their element identifiers.

-----

**Outputs**

- **Results** (`results.json`): per raw file its SHA-256, `status`, `error` and, when
  converted, `nexus_path`: the NeXus file's path in the project zip.
- **NOMAD projects**: one zip per Zenodo record, named by record ID, only for records with at
  least one converted raw file:

      <version DOI>/                 e.g. 10.5281_zenodo.1
        <raw file stem>/             raw file, NeXus file (<stem>.nxs) and eln_data.yaml
        Complementaries/             the record's other files (all but raw and ignored ones), at their original paths

  If two raw files have the same stem, the folder also gets the extension (`<stem>_<ext>`).
  Failed raw files are left out, so they can be converted again by a later tool version.
- **Logs**: one per record version, named after its DOI (`10.5281_zenodo.1`): archives, download
  failures, and per raw file the outcome, missing ELN fields and missing required NeXus concepts.
- **Summary**: an HTML table with the counts per record.
    ]]></help>
